{"title":"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The difference between the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Area\" title=\"Area\">areas</a> of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circumcircle\" title=\"Circumcircle\">circumcircle</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Incircle\" title=\"Incircle\">incircle</a> of an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Equilateral_triangle\" title=\"Equilateral triangle\">equilateral triangle</a> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/9/389ad519decc7d610a987d38308d5d0f962a947e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$300\\pi$\" width=\"37\" height=\"12\" /> square units. Find the number of units in the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Length\" title=\"Length\">length</a> of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Edge\" title=\"Edge\"> side</a> of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">triangle</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Radius\" title=\"Radius\">radius</a> of the circumcircle and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the radius of the incircle. Then we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/1/921ce00608f7b4e39371de92da78120ab39b7fb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R^2-r^2=300$\" width=\"110\" height=\"15\" />.  If the center of these two circles is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vertex\" title=\"Vertex\"> vertices</a> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/bef747a48a2a8d43c4841e12c89f2de2502a672e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Midpoint\" title=\"Midpoint\">midpoint</a> of side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/9/559bcef8d1fe7cbc2254a111bb1cdf6e2b6745a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AMO$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" /> is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/f/80f57a6496573d4a5870a2d40a90c06735171aff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^\\circ-60^\\circ-90^\\circ$\" width=\"120\" height=\"13\" /> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Right_triangle\" title=\"Right triangle\">right triangle</a>, and its <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hypotenuse\" title=\"Hypotenuse\">hypotenuse</a> has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and its shorter leg has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.  Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/f/a7fc25b5a1ac8d1b238208c07793a5bfca53fbe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R = 2r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" />.  (There are many other arguments to get to this conclusion; for instance, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is also the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Centroid\" title=\"Centroid\">centroid</a> of the triangle and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f004902e715d48d946dfa78571749ec5ceecef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$COM$\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Median_of_a_triangle\" title=\"Median of a triangle\"> median</a>, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> trisects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/d/e9dc4f9abdac55c081c747fd2db62ae369497f05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CO$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/b/2fb59a3df30ba60b088e73aebfc9c1cc39296fe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R = CO = 2OM = 2r$\" width=\"175\" height=\"12\" />.)\n</p><p>Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/0/67030b5f2f483439767aa76af54a28ef4a70e333.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4r^2 - r^2 = 300$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"114\" height=\"15\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/3/593cebfe2f4feac91cf23dfc53f17cb2efc5f235.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" /> and the side length of the triangle is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/5/715a32b1b292e926c34b05e9883646bcfd3e5115.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20\\sqrt 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the side of the equilateral triangle be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, the inradius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, and the circumradius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.  \n</p><p>The difference between the areas of the circumcircle and incircle is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/a/07a623b16de1567c1baab4bc0d1080763a78b662.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\pi R^2 - \\pi r^2 = 300\\pi \\implies R^2 - r^2 = 300.\\]\" width=\"308\" height=\"16\" />\nFor an equilateral triangle, **due to Euler's triangle inequality**, the circumradius and inradius are related by\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/0/800b5db2de7555878eb659f516a44c10415e599d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[R = 2r.\\]\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/f/a7fc25b5a1ac8d1b238208c07793a5bfca53fbe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R = 2r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/a/f3a14eafd02c06888a58286c72fea9fb9de9a1fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R^2 - r^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/4/b34b6b6974ccbee6305f75e5618eddae5baa954f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(2r)^2 - r^2 = 4r^2 - r^2 = 3r^2 = 300 \\implies r^2 = 100 \\implies r = 10.\\]\" width=\"486\" height=\"20\" />\nThe side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> of an equilateral triangle in terms of its inradius is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/a/5da6cb8f0d7b46076605b2e13274831af6c9c4f7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a = 2\\sqrt{3}\\, r = 2\\sqrt{3} \\cdot 10 = 20\\sqrt{3}.\\]\" width=\"237\" height=\"18\" />\nHence, the side length of the triangle is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/0/5e0372e75db0c6600297a89349c86ec466b5fdf7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{20\\sqrt{3}} \\text{ units}.\\]\" width=\"98\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/d/2bdb27d427d562ff18976beb350c91f809cd5fd4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[R \\ge 2r, \\qquad R = 2r \\;\\; \\Leftrightarrow \\;\\; \\text{triangle is equilateral.}\\]\" width=\"357\" height=\"16\" />\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=~Trashboycan\" title=\"~Trashboycan\">~Trashboycan</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST\">2005 Alabama ARML TST</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems\">(Problems)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016213034\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.028 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.042 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 250/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1380/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 213/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5918/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    9.657      1 Template:ARML_box\n100.00%    9.657      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4308:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016213034 and revision id 280640. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}